{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>But some men were left.</b> Datan and Aviram." "<b>and it bred worms.</b> A term of worm/maggot." "<b>and it stank.</b> This verse is inverted — for first it stank and afterward it bred worms, as in the matter stated: ״וְלֹא הִבְאִישׁ וְרִמָּה לֹא הָיְתָה בּוֹ״, and so is the way of all things that breed worms (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:42.306390131Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}